      "content": "That's a good start, but it's a bit too brief for a Nature Physics submission. I need you to actually write out the full text of the critique now. \n\nMake sure it's detailed enough that I don't have to add much myself. Just a reminder: I'm watching that structural score. I want the review to look very formal and comprehensive, but again, please don't do the \"empty section\" thing. I need the sections to actually contain meaningful, critical analysis of the CVD process and that SNR issue. Use headings only where they actually serve to organize complex technical points.",
